{{!-- Trageslots: carried gear packed into the slot budget. The layout is
derived on every render from the items' existing sort order — nothing about
the arrangement is stored — so reordering is purely a view concern.

Worn clothing and armour never appear here: "Von den Inventarregeln
ausgenommen sind Kleidung und Rüstung welche der Charakter am Leib trägt".
The grid holds exactly as many cells as the character has slots; there is no
padding out to the raster width. Anything past the budget keeps running on in
the same grid, marked over capacity. --}}
<div class='basics-section-header slot-grid-header'>
    <h3 class='basics-section-title slot-grid-title'>{{localize 'TNO.Inventory.CarrySlots'}}</h3>
    {{!-- Used over capacity. The three parts are separate elements because they
    rank differently — the figure the player tracks, the separator, the limit
    behind it — and the container is a flex row, so the newlines between them
    collapse away rather than becoming spaces around the slash. --}}
    <span class='slot-grid-count'>
      <strong{{#if slotGrid.over}} class='over-capacity'{{/if}}>{{slotGrid.used}}</strong>
      <span class='slot-grid-sep' aria-hidden='true'>/</span>
      <span class='slot-grid-max'>{{slotGrid.capacity}}</span>
    </span>

    {{!-- What the load costs in movement is shown on the movement chip in the
    banner, struck through the tier it takes away — the question it answers is
    "how far can I move", so it belongs on the numbers, not over the bag.
    "Keine Tasche" stays here: it is not a load level but the reason this whole
    budget reads 0, and nowhere else says so. --}}
    {{#ifEquals slotGrid.state 'noContainer'}}
      <span class='slot-badge badge-no-container' title='{{localize "TNO.Inventory.NoContainerHint"}}'>
        {{localize 'TNO.Inventory.NoContainer'}}
      </span>
    {{/ifEquals}}

    {{#if @root.editable}}
      <a class='inventory-add' title='{{localize "TNO.Inventory.AddHint"}}'>
        <i class='fas fa-plus'></i>
      </a>
    {{/if}}
</div>

<div class='slot-grid-block card basics-section-card'>

  {{!-- One cell per slot the load costs, in one flat run: what fits, then what
  spills past the budget, then — only when nothing spilled — the free cells.
  A multi-slot item is several adjacent cells joined by CSS rather than one
  element spanning columns, so it can wrap mid-item instead of jumping to the
  next row and holding the columns behind it open.

  `draggable` is the class core's DragDrop binds, which is what puts the item
  on the drag payload: without it a cell drags as an empty ghost. Every cell of
  a block carries the id so it can be grabbed and dropped onto along its whole
  length; `_onSortItem` is overridden to fold the repeats back into one
  sibling. Dragging a cell onto another sorts the list, onto a free cell moves
  it to the end, and armour dragged onto its paper doll zone is worn. --}}
  <div class='slot-grid'>
    {{#each slotGrid.cells as |cell|}}
      <div class='slot-cell slot-filled draggable{{#if cell.over}} over-capacity{{/if}}{{#if cell.first}} slot-first{{/if}}{{#unless cell.last}} slot-joined{{/unless}}'
           style='--slot-run: {{cell.span}}'
           data-item-id='{{cell.item._id}}'
           data-tooltip-html='{{cell.tip}}'
           data-tooltip-direction='UP'>
        {{#if cell.first}}
          <i class='fas fa-grip-vertical slot-grip'></i>
          {{#if cell.over}}<i class='fas fa-triangle-exclamation slot-overflow-icon'></i>{{/if}}
          <img class='slot-icon' src='{{cell.item.img}}' width='16' height='16' alt=''/>
          <span class='slot-name'>{{cell.item.name}}</span>
          {{#if cell.showQty}}<span class='slot-qty'>×{{cell.quantity}}</span>{{/if}}
        {{/if}}
      </div>
    {{/each}}

    {{#each slotGrid.emptyCells}}
      <div class='slot-cell slot-empty'
           data-tooltip-html='{{localize "TNO.Inventory.EmptyCellHint"}}'
           data-tooltip-direction='UP'></div>
    {{/each}}
  </div>

  {{!-- Keyed off the budget, not off `overflow`: a block that merely straddles
  the boundary is packed rather than pushed out, so the load can run over
  capacity with nothing in `overflow` at all — which is precisely when this
  needs saying. --}}
  {{#if slotGrid.over}}
    <p class='slot-grid-note slot-grid-overflow-note'>
      {{localize 'TNO.Inventory.Overflow' excess=slotGrid.excess}}
    </p>
  {{/if}}


</div>
